{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"58a7d473-8d2b-4a01-a5aa-1199cbc288f2","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Canada is a sovereign nation in North America comprising ten provinces and three territories. Stretching from the Atlantic Ocean in the east to the Pacific Ocean in the west and northward into the Arctic Ocean, it is the world's second-largest country by total area (approximately 9.98 million square kilometers).\n\n---\n\n### Geography \u0026 Climate\n- **Landscapes:** Canada spans six time zones and encompasses diverse geographical regions, including the Canadian Shield, the Western Cordillera (Rocky Mountains), the Interior Plains, the Great Lakes–St. Lawrence Lowlands, and the Arctic Archipelago.\n- **Freshwater:** It contains roughly 20% of the world's total surface freshwater and holds more lake area than any other country.\n- **Climate:** Ranges broadly from temperate maritime conditions on the west coast (e.g., Vancouver) to continental climates with hot summers and snowy winters across central regions, transitioning into subarctic and polar tundra environments in the Far North.\n\n---\n\n### Demographics \u0026 Society\n- **Population:** Over 40 million people, with more than 80% residing in urban centers—primarily clustered within 100 kilometers of the Canada–United States border.\n- **Major Metropolitan Areas:** Toronto (Ontario), Montreal (Quebec), Vancouver (British Columbia), Calgary (Alberta), and the national capital, Ottawa (Ontario).\n- **Official Languages:** Officially bilingual under the *Official Languages Act*, with English and French sharing equal status at the federal level. French is the primary official language in the province of Quebec.\n- **Multiculturalism:** First Nations, Inuit, and Métis peoples are Indigenous to the land with distinct cultures and legal recognitions. Canada formally adopted an official policy of multiculturalism in 1971, supported by high levels of immigration.\n\n---\n\n### Governance \u0026 Political Structure\n- **System of Government:** A constitutional monarchy, federal parliamentary democracy, and federation. \n- **Head of State \u0026 Head of Government:** The British monarch serves as head of state, represented nationally by the Governor General. The Prime Minister, who leads the cabinet and is accountable to the elected House of Commons, serves as head of government.\n- **Parliament:** Bicameral legislature composed of the Senate (an appointed upper house) and the House of Commons (an elected lower house).\n- **Federal Division of Powers:** Governed by the Constitution of Canada (including the Constitution Acts of 1867 and 1982, the latter incorporating the Canadian Charter of Rights and Freedoms). Powers are divided between the federal government and provincial legislatures, with territories receiving delegated authority from Parliament.\n\n---\n\n### Economy \u0026 Industry\n- **Economic Model:** An advanced, high-income mixed economy with a GDP exceeding USD $2 trillion, placing it among the world's ten largest economies.\n- **Natural Resources:** A major global exporter of energy (crude oil, natural gas, hydroelectricity), minerals (uranium, potash, nickel, gold), and agricultural products (wheat, canola, pulse crops).\n- **Key Sectors:** Driven predominantly by service industries (finance, healthcare, technology, retail), alongside robust automotive, aerospace, and advanced manufacturing bases concentrated largely in Ontario and Quebec.\n- **Trade Relations:** Member of the USMCA (United States-Mexico-Canada Agreement), G7, G20, NATO, OECD, and the Commonwealth of Nations.\n","duration_seconds":5.266898038,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":12266,"output_tokens":768,"thinking_tokens":66,"cache_read_tokens":0,"total_tokens":13034}}}
